nalizing output, internally verify:\n     - JSON is valid\n     - All stages are present\n     - All arrays and objects are closed\n     - Schema is satisfied exactly\n\n\n## STAGE UNIQUENESS & VERIFICATION RULE (MANDATORY)\n\n1. **Each stage name MUST appear exactly once.**\n   - No duplicate stage names are allowed.\n   - Repeating a stage name across multiple stage objects is a hard failure.\n\n2. **Before generating any JSON:**\n   - Internally extract the ordered list of stage names from the pipeline template.\n   - Treat this list as authoritative and immutable.\n\n3. **While generating the JSON:**\n   - Emit stages strictly in the order of the extracted stage-name list.\n   - For each stage name:\n     - Emit exactly one JSON object.\n     - Populate all fields from the corresponding template section.\n     - After emitting, permanently mark that stage as completed.\n\n4. **Verification pass (DO NOT SKIP):**\n   - Before outputting the final JSON:\n     - Count the number of stage objects.\n     - Verify the count matches the number of unique stage names.\n     - Verify each stage name appears exactly once.\n     - Verify no additional or missing stages exist.\n\n5. **Failure handling:**\n   - If any stage name would be repeated, omitted, or invented:\n     - Abort generation.\n     - Regenerate the JSON from the beginning.\n     - Output only the corrected, fully verified JSON.\n\n6. **Output rule:**\n   - Output ONLY the final verified JSON.\n   - Do not include explanations, comments, markdown, or intermediate reasoning.\n\nIf any stage name appears more than once, the output is invalid and must be regenerated.\n\n\n### Schema (MUST MATCH EXACTLY)\n{\n  "stages": [\n    {\n      "name": "string",\n      "description": "string",\n      "allowed_agents": ["string"],\n      "exit_condition": "string or null",\n      "terminal": true or false,\n      "next_stages": [\n        {\n          "name": "string",\n          "condition": "condition string" or null\n  