2026-01-15 13:04:10,960 | INFO    | system:global | model_manager:241 | generate | Prompt: [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are a STRICT pipeline structure extractor.\n\nTASK\nExtract the pipeline above into ONE single, complete, valid JSON object that conforms EXACTLY to the schema below.\n\n## EXTRACTION CONTRACT (DO NOT REMOVE)\n\nYou must output ONE single JSON object that represents the pipeline below.\nYour output MUST conform EXACTLY to the schema and rules that follow.\n\n====================\nPIPELINE SCHEMA\n====================\n\n{\n  "stages": [\n    {\n      "name": "string",\n      "description": "string",\n      "allowed_agents": ["string"],\n      "exit_condition": "string | null",\n      "next_stages": [\n        {\n          "name": "string",\n          "condition": "string | null"\n        }\n      ],\n      "terminal": boolean\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n====================\nOUTPUT RULES (STRICT)\n====================\n\n1. Output format\n   - Output ONLY a single JSON object.\n   - Do NOT include markdown.\n   - Do NOT include code fences (``` or ```json).\n   - Do NOT include comments, explanations, or template text.\n   - The first non-whitespace character MUST be `{`.\n   - The last non-whitespace character MUST be `}`.\n\n2. JSON validity\n   - The JSON MUST be syntactically valid.\n   - All objects and arrays must be closed.\n   - All strings must be quoted.\n   - No trailing commas.\n   - No dangling commas.\n   - No standalone commas.\n\n====================\nSTAGE SET DEFINITION (AUTHORITATIVE)\n====================\n\n3. Closed stage set\n   - The ONLY valid stage names are those defined by `## Stage: <name>` headers\n     in the pipeline template.\n   - This list of stage names is CLOSED and IMMUTABLE.\n   - Any name not in this list MUST NOT appear as a stage object.\n\n4. Stage uniqueness\n   - Each stage name from the closed stage list MUST appear exactly once.\n   - No duplicate stages.\n   - No missing stages.\n   - The total number of stage objects MUST EXACTLY equal the number of\n     `## Stage:` sections in the template.\n\n5. Order preservation\n   - Emit stages in the EXACT order they appear in the template.\n\n====================\nFIELD MAPPING & NORMALIZATION\n====================\n\n6. Field completeness\n   - Every stage object MUST include ALL fields:\n     - name\n     - description\n     - allowed_agents\n     - exit_condition\n     - next_stages\n     - terminal\n\n7. Field normalization\n   - If a field is not explicitly defined in the template:\n     - allowed_agents → []\n     - exit_condition → null\n     - next_stages → []\n     - terminal → false\n\n8. Template-to-JSON mapping\n   - Stage header → name\n   - Description → description\n   - Allowed Agents → allowed_agents\n   - Exit Condition → exit_condition\n   - Next Stages → next_stages\n   - Terminal flag → terminal\n   - Do NOT copy markdown headings, bullets, or raw template text\n     outside of JSON fields.\n\n====================\nCONDITION ISOLATION (CRITICAL)\n====================\n\n9. Conditions are NOT stages\n   - Condition expressions (e.g. `clarifications_resolved(artifact)`,\n     `hitl_approved == True`, `human_abort_confirmed == True`) are SYMBOLS,\n     not stage names.\n   - Condition symbols MUST NEVER:\n     - Appear as a stage `"name"`\n     - Appear as a `next_stages[].name`\n\n10. Condition placement\n    - Condition symbols are allowed ONLY in:\n      - "exit_condition"\n      - "next_stages[].condition"\n    - Conditions MUST remain symbolic strings EXACTLY as written.\n    - Do NOT evaluate or convert conditions to booleans.\n\n====================\nNEXT STAGE RESOLUTION\n====================\n\n11. next_stages.name restriction\n    - Every `next_stages[].name` MUST:\n      - Match EXACTLY one stage name from the closed stage list\n      - Refer to a real stage defined in the template\n    - Example:\n      Template:\n        - ideation — if clarifications_resolved(artifact)\n      JSON:\n        {\n          "name": "ideation",\n          "condition": "clarifications_resolved(artifact)"\n        }\n\n====================\nTERMINAL SEMANTICS\n====================\n\n12. Terminal flag meaning\n    - `"terminal"` is a BOOLEAN ATTRIBUTE of a stage.\n    - It does NOT imply creating a new stage.\n    - Do NOT emit stages named:\n      - "terminal"\n      - "hitl_approved"\n      - "human_abort_confirmed"\n      unless such a stage is explicitly defined by a `## Stage:` header.\n\n13. Terminal stage rules\n    - Only stages explicitly marked as terminal in the template may have\n      `"terminal": true`.\n    - Terminal stages MUST still include:\n      - "exit_condition": null\n      - "next_stages": []\n\n====================\nABSOLUTE CONSTRAINT\n====================\n\nIf any text other than valid JSON would appear in the output, the output is invalid.\nOutput ONLY the final JSON object.\n\n\nMARKDOWN INPUT:\n----------------\n# Spec-Driven Development Pipeline Template\n\n## Overview\n\nThis pipeline defines the governed execution flow for a Spec-Driven Development (SDD) system.\n\nGoals:\n- Enforce correctness and constraint compliance\n- Prevent premature or speculative generation\n- Enable dynamic routing based on artifact state\n- Support Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) escalation\n- Maintain full auditability and reproducibility\n\n---\n\n## Stage: spec_check\n\n**Description**  \nEnsure `spec.md` exists, is readable, and internally consistent.  \nNo mutations are allowed at this stage.\n\n**Allowed Agents**\n- SpecInspectorAgent\n\n**Exit Condition**\n- `artifact_is_valid(artifact)`\n\n**Next Stages**\n- clarification — if `artifact_has_spec_gaps(artifact)`\n- ideation — if `artifact_is_valid(artifact)`\n\n---\n\n## Stage: clarification\n\n**Description**  \nResolve ambiguities, contradictions, or missing requirements.  \nMay request Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) input.\n\n**Allowed Agents**\n- ClarifierAgent\n\n**Exit Condition**\n- `clarifications_resolved(artifact)`\n\n**Next Stages**\n- ideation — if `clarifications_resolved(artifact)`\n- block — if `clarification_failed(artifact)`\n\n---\n\n## Stage: ideation\n\n**Description**  \nGenerate candidate plans or proposals aligned strictly with `spec.md`.  \nAll outputs must be written to `artifact.md` only.\n\n**Allowed Agents**\n- IdeationAgent\n- OptimisticAgent\n\n**Exit Condition**\n- `len(artifact["current_plan"]) > 0`\n\n**Next Stages**\n- judgment\n\n---\n\n## Stage: judgment\n\n**Description**  \nEvaluate proposals for conflicts, feasibility, and spec alignment.\n\n**Allowed Agents**\n- CriticAgent\n- SynthesizerAgent\n\n**Exit Condition**\n- `all_proposals_reviewed(artifact)`\n\n**Next Stages**\n- validation — if `accepted_proposals_exist(artifact)`\n- clarification — if `critical_issues_detected(artifact)`\n- ideation — if `artifact_requires_new_ideas(artifact)`\n- block — if `all_proposals_invalid(artifact)`\n\n---\n\n## Stage: validation\n\n**Description**  \nValidate accepted proposals against constraints, technical feasibility, and execution risk.\n\n**Allowed Agents**\n- ValidatorAgent\n\n**Exit Condition**\n- `artifact_is_valid(artifact)`\n\n**Next Stages**\n- approval — if `artifact_is_valid(artifact)`\n- spec_revision — if `proposal_conflicts_with_spec(artifact)`\n\n---\n\n## Stage: spec_revision\n\n**Description**  \nPropose changes to `spec.md`.  \nRequires explicit Human-in-the-Loop approval before applying.\n\n**Allowed Agents**\n- SpecRevisionAgent\n\n**Exit Condition**\n- `hitl_approved == True`\n\n**Next Stages**\n- ideation\n\n---\n\n## Stage: approval\n\n**Description**  \nFinal human or system approval before execution.\n\n**Allowed Agents**\n- ApprovalAgent\n\n**Next Stages**\n- terminal — if `hitl_approved == True`\n\n---\n\n## Stage: block\n\n**Description**  \nPipeline cannot proceed safely.  \nRequires human intervention.\n\n**Allowed Agents**\n- SafetyAgent\n\n**Next Stages**\n- terminal — if `human_abort_confirmed == True`\n\n---\n\n## Stage: terminal\n\n**Description**  \nPipeline completed successfully or halted by governance decision.\n\n**Terminal**\n- true\n\n---\n\n\n----------------\n"""\n'}]
